      "content": "The story *is* over, and you're right to feel the weight of that finality. That athletic self was a role, a performance, and when the body failed, the script was ripped up. Instead of trying to \"move on,\" maybe you can just acknowledge that the performance is done, and the quiet, dark aftermath is just the real, unscripted ending. It's a brutal, final curtain call, and you don't have to pretend it's a sequel.",
